hello my name is alvin and today i'll be  showing you guys my recipe for the best  fudgy brownies ever  [Music]  so box mix brownies they're great  there's nothing against them they're  awesome but the thing is i wanted  something that was a little bit  different i didn't want the recipe to be  just something you could get out of a  box i want the funniest brownies ever i  want a lot of chocolate in there i want  it to be warm and gooey when you eat it  i want people to take a bite and be like  oh damn this fudgy af so i set off to  make the fudgiest brownies ever it  requires a lot of chocolate which is a  great thing and i think the most  important thing is that you make sure  that all of your ingredients are evenly  combined make sure that your eggs are  actually whisked a little bit more than  usual because you want to beat a little  bit of air into them to get that really  silky texture that was one thing that i  learned from testing was that if you  beat your eggs a little bit more than  normal you're going to get a lot  creamier sort of base that will make the  brownie a lot fudgier  another thing i would say is that don't  use just any chocolate bar you find at  the store try to make sure you get  really good chocolate because it will  make the difference you will taste the  difference and try to get a little bit  extra because i always found myself  eating at least half a bar before the  recipe was even done so definitely have  some extra chocolate on hand to snack on  because you're gonna need it  i really think that people love baking  brownies i think it's such a fun  activity baking is something that  innately requires you to go hang out  with a friend like i really wanted a  recipe that people could use as a way to  invite other people to hang out with  them i like being able to see these nice  gooey pools of chocolate on top so i'm  gonna save some chocolate and also put  some chunks on top of the brownie at the  end because i think when it comes out of  the oven you know like this is a legit  brownie this didn't come from a box this  came from your own hands and your  friends are going to go crazy and people  are going to want you to share but i  don't want you to share it even though  if you want to share because i ate the  whole tray one time and i did not regret  a single thing you want to make sure  that your brownies are baked but not  over baked because when you take it  right out of the oven it might seem like  a little soft in the center not  everything's set and that's okay because  there's a lot of chocolate in there and  that's going to be melted at that point  what you want to do which would be the  probably the hardest part to do in this  entire recipe is to wait you need to  wait for it to cool down completely  because even when it cools down  completely the chocolate won't harden if  it's really good chocolate it there  should be some gooeyness some liquidity  as it cools so even when you cut into it  and it's not warm anymore you'll still  have these nice gooey pools of chocolate  it's your recipe you can do whatever you  want with it you can add nuts you can  add caramel you can add whatever you  like just be sure that once you put more  toppings in you're going to need to bake  it for a little bit longer because now  you're preventing the batter from rising  and cooking as fast as it usually would  so if you add something in just bake it  a little more and honestly brownies are  great no matter what if you want to be a  little fancy and you have some coarse or  flaky sea salt on hand sprinkle a little  bit of salt on the brownies while  they're still hot so the salt becomes a  part of the brownie as it cools and when  you cut it that salt is going to be this  really nice touch that counteracts the  flavor and the sweetness of the  chocolate  [Music]  make sure you pour yourself a really  nice glass of cold milk because you  can't have brownies without milk just  like cookies i love this recipe i think  it's a great base recipe for any brownie  that you want to make so if you do make  it if you have a variation on it if you  add crazy things in i want to know too  so let me know post in the comments and  i want to see your stuff i love to see  when people make my recipes so  happy baking  [Music]  you
 

